@page
@model MossHarper.Pages.PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy information";
}
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow light">Privacy information</p><h1>How contact enquiries are handled.</h1></div></section>
<section class="section-pad"><div class="container prose"><p>When you use the contact form, we collect the name, email address, organisation and role (if provided), and message you submit. We use that information to review and respond to your enquiry.</p><p>The form sends your message through Gmail SMTP to the business recipients configured for Moss Harper. The website does not keep a separate database of enquiries. Please do not include sensitive personal information or confidential documents in an initial enquiry.</p><p>For questions about how an enquiry is handled, please use the <a asp-page="/Contact" asp-fragment="contact">contact form</a>.</p></div></section>
